      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. It has no recognized indication, and it carries a real risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen. If you think this patient has an unusual indication that needs a dose above the maximum, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy first. The order can then go through your hospital's override process.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
